# [DD-13b.W23.4] S243 (S-R4b)'s own detector: one block, two `m` case
# lines. On the shipped schema `m` is NOT a block opener, so this is one
# `pattern` row and two #section cases rows. Under S243's plant (a THIRD
# member added to `opens_group`, `m`) each `m` line closes the block
# above it and opens a NEW one — three `pattern` rows and ZERO case
# rows, since every `m` line is consumed as an opener rather than
# dispatched as a case.
pattern a
m "x" 0 1
m "y" 0 1
